{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06DP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$x \\in |X|$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$x$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$x$", "MATH_0009": "$Y$", "MATH_0010": "$f(x)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descend-unibranch}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:10fe351bb3df4c885b2e4cc325514595b56cfa6c584f00158cadfe21d97c655b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:274ad3c18401f5868ff1a742d2999f03ac7b4eee1fff3e8e12711986df7f85b3", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004>.\nIf <MATH_0005> is flat at <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007> is geometrically unibranch at <MATH_0008>, then <MATH_0009> is\ngeometrically unibranch at <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2e29f4b217c8de36f5619080675067225e479ceba039729d00533fc51f771eb2", "unit_id": "tag:06DQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06DP", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(\\overline{x})} \\to \\mathcal{O}_{X, \\overline{x}}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, \\overline{x}}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(\\overline{x})}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-flat-at-point-etale-local-rings}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-flat-going-down}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b83bd94267cd518748405ec05ab0b15f7c565f82c02a04a1fbb64c335e39ad08", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:89f6c3721d1cd98804db37b15ed1f46e8088d6d30e9a7f70e93cb17bb4971fc7", "source_text": "Consider the map of <ACCENT_0001>tale local rings\n<MATH_0001>.\nBy\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>\nthis is flat. Hence if <MATH_0002> has a unique minimal\nprime, so does <MATH_0003> (by going down, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0002>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f15a6272980672360b4c17bab5ddfb455de96b79ab46f7a93f47b5087ad66fe8", "unit_id": "tag:06DQ:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06DP", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nA flat and surjective morphism of algebraic spaces with a reduced source\nhas a reduced target.\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$Y$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descend-reduced}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b02e6fd76257d07ab1de01ae19306203466627792e764b752eacc4f8e2409ec1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b2744301ecaf58dbc093f2954224b228babe71e257723cc0480871a5c053cde4", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>.\nIf <MATH_0004> is flat and surjective and <MATH_0005> is reduced, then <MATH_0006> is reduced.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a87f4a1116f0f0bf3c3caa7f0c29c5a525e316d51b64428b7d20a61b29ee1131", "unit_id": "tag:06MI:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06DP", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$V$", "MATH_0002": "$V \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to X \\times_Y V$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to V$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$Y$", "MATH_0009": "$U$", "MATH_0010": "$V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-properties-section-types-properties}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{descent-lemma-descend-reduced}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4d4f06c009394af9e771176cf978ab35ebabe56425750b9efd756a4af4eb4bba", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d78655cfad02189f810a473dba668b17bb79bbcbdf15cde254a98844ef0213b8", "source_text": "Choose a scheme <MATH_0001> and a surjective <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism <MATH_0002>.\nChoose a scheme <MATH_0003> and a surjective <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism\n<MATH_0004>. As <MATH_0005> is surjective and flat, the morphism of\nschemes <MATH_0006> is surjective and flat. In this way we reduce the\nproblem to the case of schemes (as reducedness of <MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008> is defined\nin terms of reducedness of <MATH_0009> and <MATH_0010>, see\nProperties of Spaces,\nSection <REF_0001>).\nThe case of schemes is\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:543cd1fced13ced35514c71565639ded66810beda6f2f99b6b5fd47b11bd56dd", "unit_id": "tag:06MI:proof"}
